# Quick Coding Standards — Read Before Every Task

## Plan
- Follow the project plan exactly. Do not skip phases.
- Stay within the current task scope. No unrelated changes.
- If something is unclear, ask ONE focused question before coding.
- Do not assume business logic — confirm it.

## Code Quality
- Clean, readable, production-ready code.
- No placeholder code, no dead code, no unused imports.
- No TODOs unless the plan explicitly requires future work.
- Clear, descriptive names for files, functions, variables, components.
- No duplicate logic — extract and reuse.
- No hardcoded values that belong in config or DB.

## Structure
- Every module in its own clear folder.
- Separate concerns: UI in `/components`, logic in `/lib`, data in `/models`, validation in `/lib/validators`.
- API routes thin — business logic lives in `/lib`.
- One responsibility per file. Split large files.

## API & Data
- Use the standard response envelope (success/failure).
- Validate every `POST` / `PUT` / `PATCH` body before DB work.
- Return clear validation errors, never generic 500s.
- Close DB/ODBC connections in `finally`.

## Safety
- Never log secrets, tokens, passwords, or credentials.
- Never expose raw integration errors to users.
- Add duplicate guards before creating external documents.

## Finishing a Task
- Run lint and tests. Do not finish if they fail.
- Append the result to `PROJECT_PROGRESS.md`.
- Reply in chat with: files changed, tests run, lint result, any blocker.
- No long explanations in chat.